I was playing 3.0i today on my school's computer (I dont knwo why they
havent gotten 3.1.1), and I made a dumb move.  A classic dumb move.
A dumb move that has surely been made thousands of times before.

"Well, lets throw all thius crap into this bag of holding, then I can
carry this bones pile... Good idea Dan!  Wait though!  Lets look and
see if we have a wand of cancellation first!  We dont want to make
that mistake again ha ha!.. Nope, no wand of cancel! Were safe!
Go ahead, hit 'a' in response to that prompt!"

Of course, I didnt think about the bag of tricks.  And I realized it
the second I hit the key.  what should I have done?  I hit
Cntrl-C, and it asked me if I wanted to quit, and stopped listing things,
but was frozen until I hit return, upon which it would start listing
the soon-to-be-destroyed goodis.  Is there anything I could have done?
Hung up the phone so that it would save, and maybe not have been in the
middle of listing when I logged back on?

I really had an awesome game going.  I had 3 wand of polymorph,
had polypiled everything a hacker could want (just about).  Had just
wiped out a barrakcs and picked up a dozen RoP ready to be piled.
Had gotten this far in the game by zapping my doggie into a Vampire lord
on the first try in the first room.

When my I lost my goodeis to my bag, (which was my weight-bug bag BTW)
I lost my heart to play with it.  I got killed by an invisble stalker
5 mins later, having lost the desire to play (or check my HP when
fighting after removing all my armor).

sigh.

